{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "O95971", "secondaryAccessions": ["A0A0B4J2A1", "B8PRF2", "Q5T2V6"], "uniProtkbId": "BY55_HUMAN", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "2001-10-18", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-06-10", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "1999-05-01", "entryVersion": 195, "sequenceVersion": 1}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Homo sapiens", "commonName": "Human", "taxonId": 9606, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Metazoa", "Chordata", "Craniata", "Vertebrata", "Euteleostomi", "Mammalia", "Eutheria", "Euarchontoglires", "Primates", "Haplorrhini", "Catarrhini", "Hominidae", "Homo"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"value": "CD160 antigen"}}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"value": "Natural killer cell receptor BY55"}}], "cdAntigenNames": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16809620"}], "value": "CD160"}], "contains": [{"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "17237375"}], "value": "CD160 antigen, soluble form"}}}], "flag": "Precursor"}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16809620"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000312", "source": "HGNC", "id": "HGNC:17013"}], "value": "CD160"}, "synonyms": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9743336"}], "value": "BY55"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "O88875"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11978774"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12486241"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16809620"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "17307798"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "18193050"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "19109136"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "25255144"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9973372"}], "value": "Receptor on immune cells capable to deliver stimulatory or inhibitory signals that regulate cell activation and differentiation. Exists as a GPI-anchored and as a transmembrane form, each likely initiating distinct signaling pathways via phosphoinositol 3-kinase in activated NK cells and via LCK and CD247/CD3 zeta chain in activated T cells (PubMed:11978774, PubMed:17307798, PubMed:19109136). Receptor for both classical and non-classical MHC class I molecules (PubMed:12486241, PubMed:9973372). In the context of acute viral infection, recognizes HLA-C and triggers NK cell cytotoxic activity, likely playing a role in anti-viral innate immune response (PubMed:12486241). On CD8+ T cells, binds HLA-A2-B2M in complex with a viral peptide and provides a costimulatory signal to activated/memory T cells (PubMed:9973372). Upon persistent antigen stimulation, such as occurs during chronic viral infection, may progressively inhibit TCR signaling in memory CD8+ T cells, contributing to T cell exhaustion (PubMed:25255144). On endothelial cells, recognizes HLA-G and controls angiogenesis in immune privileged sites (PubMed:16809620). Receptor or ligand for TNF superfamily member TNFRSF14, participating in bidirectional cell-cell contact signaling between antigen presenting cells and lymphocytes. Upon ligation of TNFRSF14, provides stimulatory signal to NK cells enhancing IFNG production and anti-tumor immune response (By similarity). On activated CD4+ T cells, interacts with TNFRSF14 and down-regulates CD28 costimulatory signaling, restricting memory and alloantigen-specific immune response (PubMed:18193050). In the context of bacterial infection, acts as a ligand for TNFRSF14 on epithelial cells, triggering the production of antimicrobial proteins and pro-inflammatory cytokines (By similarity)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION", "molecule": "CD160 antigen"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "17237375"}], "value": "The soluble GPI-cleaved form, usually released by activated lymphocytes, might play an immune regulatory role by limiting lymphocyte effector functions"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION", "molecule": "CD160 antigen, soluble form"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11978774"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16809620"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "18193050"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9973372"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9743336"}], "value": "Homomultimer; disulfide-linked (Probable). Interacts with HLA-G (PubMed:16809620). Interacts with HLA-A2-B2M in complex with an HIV-derived peptide (PubMed:9973372). Interacts with TNFRSF14 (via cysteine-rich domain 1); this interaction is direct (PubMed:18193050). Interacts with LCK and CD247/CD3 zeta chain (PubMed:11978774)"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "INTERACTION", "interactions": [{"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "O95971", "intActId": "EBI-4314390"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q6RW13", "geneName": "AGTRAP", "intActId": "EBI-741181"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "O95971", "intActId": "EBI-4314390"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q96DZ9-2", "geneName": "CMTM5", "intActId": "EBI-11522780"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "O95971", "intActId": "EBI-4314390"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q9NX76", "geneName": "CMTM6", "intActId": "EBI-1054315"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "O95971", "intActId": "EBI-4314390"}, "interactantTw